}}|subdivision_type1=[[Communities of Balisca|Community]]|subdivision_name1={{flag|Araucaria}}|area_km2=114731.29|population_census=2,028,295|population_census_year=2025|regional_languages=|common_languages=[[Mozbayani]], [[Baliscano]], [[Maroniko language|Maroniko]] and [[Classical Aruanãyára language|Aruanãyára]]|cctld=.jru|government_type={{W|Liquid democracy}}|ethnic_groups=86.8% [[Baliscans]]<br/> 13.2% [[Demographics of Balisca|others]]|ethnic_groups_year=2023|mapsize=280px|population_census_rank=24th}}'''Jaguarundi''' ({{Langx|tpn|yawaum'di|4=place of {{W|jaguarundi|dark jaguar}}}}; {{Langx|mxi|خَاغْوَارُونْدِي|J̌aḡwaruńdí}}) is a rugged and mountainous coastal region in western [[Araucaria]], and one of the [[regions of Balisca|seven regions]] of the [[Communities of Balisca|community]]. It borders [[Kamakã]] and [[Llaragón]] to the north and [[Tukupi]] to the south.

It has an area of {{convert|114731.29|km2|abbr=on}} making it the [[List of Baliscan regions by area|x-largest region of Balisca by area]]. According to the [[2025 Baliscan census]], Jaguarundi had a population of 2,028,295. The administrative center of Jaguarundi is [[Porciúncula]], while [[Calatañazor]] is its most populous city.

The region has a {{W|humid subtropical climate}}, characterized by hot, humid summers and mild to cool winters. 

